    <node id="own electric wheelchair">
      <data key="d0">query</data>
      <data key="d1">own electric wheelchair</data>
      <data key="d2">...own electric wheelchair,</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Namaskara from Bangalore International Airport Limited. Thank you for contacting us. If you are travelling with your own electric wheelchair, please inform your respective airline in advance so they can coordinate the required process and approvals with BLR Airport. For wheelchair assistance, the request should be placed at the time of booking or at least 48 hours before travel. **Wheelchair Assistance** &gt; **Wheelchair Assistance** &gt; **Zone:** Special Assistance - Wheelchair Assistance &gt; Passengers requiring wheelchair assistance at BLR Airport must place a request with the respective airlines at the time of booking tickets or 48 hours prior to their travel. Passengers using personal wheelchairs are requested to contact the respective airlines in advance regarding the processes and approvals. There are dedicated zones reserved for passenger drop-off and pick-up when availing wheelchair assistance at BLR Airport. Please speak to the on-ground team for assistance. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/travellers/services/special-assistance/wheelchair-assistance) &gt; **Mobility Assist** &gt; **Zone:** Special Assistance - Mobility Assist &gt; Seamless Mobility Support for People with Disabilities. This service helps make boarding and deplaning comfortable and dignified, with smooth transfers and coordinated support in partnership with your airline. Please inform your airline at least 24 hours prior to departure. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/travellers/services/special-assistance/mobility-assist) If you would like, I can also help you with the nearest wheelchair assistance counter or the PRM drop-off locations in T1 or T2.">
      <data key="d0">chatbot_response</data>
      <data key="d1">Namaskara from Bangalore International A</data>
      <data key="d2">If you are travelling with your own electric wheelchair</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="buggy service inside terminal">
      <data key="d0">query</data>
      <data key="d1">buggy service inside terminal</data>
      <data key="d2">...buggy service inside terminal,</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Namaskara from Bangalore International Airport Limited. Thank you for contacting us. Complimentary buggy service is available inside the terminal for senior citizens, expectant mothers, passengers with reduced mobility, injury, and also for families travelling with infants and young children. It is available both at arrival and departure zones, and our ground staff can help you with it. **Terminal 1 Options** &gt; **Buggy Service** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 1 - After security check, and also at PRM drop-off locations, elevated walkway, arrival exit areas, and near baggage claim &gt; Complimentary buggy service is available for passengers who need assistance moving through the terminal. In Terminal 1, it can be found at PRM Drop-off Lane 2, PRM Drop-off Lane 3, the elevated walkway, opposite Arrival Gate 10, opposite Hamleys outlet, next to Rare Planet, Arrival Corridor near Gate A5, and Baggage Belt 07. &gt; &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/travellers/services/special-assistance/buggy-service) **Terminal 2 Options** &gt; **Buggy Service** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 2 - After security check, departure areas, arrival exit areas, and domestic arrival near baggage claim &gt; Complimentary buggy service is available in Terminal 2 for passengers who need assistance. You can ask the ground staff at Level 3 Departure Lane 1 near the PRM Drop-off Area and CarebyBLR Counter, Departure after Security near Orientation Garden, Departure Post Security near Starbucks, Arrival Exit Gates, Domestic Arrival Exit near Baggage Claim, and Level 0 Arrival Exit. &gt; &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/travellers/services/special-assistance/buggy-service) If you are already inside the terminal and need help finding the nearest buggy point, please tell me whether you are in T1 or T2, and I will guide you more precisely.">
      <data key="d0">chatbot_response</data>
      <data key="d1">Namaskara from Bangalore International A</data>
      <data key="d2">Complimentary buggy service is available inside the terminal</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="rest pods">
      <data key="d0">query</data>
      <data key="d1">rest pods</data>
      <data key="d2">... rest pods,</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Namaskara from Bangalore International Airport Limited. Thank you for contacting us. For rest or recharge in Terminal 2, the closest match I could find is the 080 Transit Hotel inside T2. It is designed for passengers who want to rest between flights, with hourly and overnight bookings available, and a minimum package of 4 hours. 080 Transit Hotel Zone: Terminal 2 - Inside Terminal 2 Located inside Bangalore Airport T2, this transit hotel is meant for long layovers, quick relief during delays, jet lag recovery, and overnight connections. It offers Deluxe Single and Double rooms, along with air conditioning, cable TV, minibar, free Wi‑Fi, a restaurant, and 24/7 service. Guests also have the option to access the 080 Lounge. Reference: Click here for more details. If you were specifically looking for a dedicated rest pod facility, I couldn’t find one in the available Terminal 2 data.">
      <data key="d0">chatbot_response</data>
      <data key="d1">Namaskara from Bangalore International A</data>
      <data key="d2">For rest or recharge in Terminal 2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="where can i find terminal map">
      <data key="d0">query</data>
      <data key="d1">where can i find terminal map</data>
      <data key="d2">...where can i find terminal map,</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Namaskara from Bangalore International Airport Limited. Thank you for contacting us. You can find the terminal map on the airport’s Indoor Map page. I’m sharing the map link below so you can open it directly and use it for navigation inside the airport. Terminal 1 Options Indoor Map Zone: Terminal 1 - Airport Map Use this map to look up airport locations and plan your movement inside the terminal. Reference: Click here for more details Terminal 2 Options Indoor Map Zone: Terminal 2 - Airport Map Use this map to look up airport locations and plan your movement inside the terminal. Reference: Click here for more details If you’d like, I can also help you with the exact location of a shop, lounge, gate, or facility on the map.">
      <data key="d0">chatbot_response</data>
      <data key="d1">Namaskara from Bangalore International A</data>
      <data key="d2">You can find the terminal map</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
