    <node id="Namaskara from Bangalore International Airport Limited. Thank you for contacting us. Yes, private car parking is available at Terminal 2. The closest parking facility is at the Arrivals level of T2, and long-term car parking is also available there. Please follow the directional signages or speak to a traffic warden for help. **Terminal 2 Options** &gt; **P2 T2 Car Parking** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 2 - Arrivals level &gt; This parking is available for private cars. The fare is 00–10 mins free, additional 30 mins ₹100, every additional 1 hour ₹50, premium parking first 24 hours ₹1000, every additional 24 hours ₹600, and loss of ticket ₹600. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/travellers/transport-parking/parking) &gt; **Long-Term Car Parking** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 2 - Arrivals level &gt; Long-term car parking facility is available at T2. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/travellers/passenger-services/faqs-about-blr-airport-bial) If you’d like, I can also help with the nearest pick-up point or electric car parking at T2.">
      <data key="d0">response</data>
      <data key="d1">Namaskara from Bangalore International A</data>
      <data key="d2">private car parking is available at Terminal 2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Namaskara from Bangalore International Airport Limited. Thank you for contacting us. If you’ve lost something at BLR, you can search for your item online and then claim it if there’s a match. The Lost &amp; Found desk is open 24/7, and claims are usually responded to within 3 business days. **Terminal 1 Options** &gt; **Lost &amp; Found** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 1 - Kerbside and Departure Hall, next to Staff Gate No. 13 &gt; You can write to **lostandfound@bialairport.com** or call **+91-8047406666** if you cannot find your item in the search. &gt; Please keep your **boarding pass**, a **valid Government photo ID**, and the **details of the item** ready when you claim it. &gt; If someone else is collecting it for you, they will also need their ID, your ID, your boarding pass, and an authorization letter from you. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/travellers/passenger-services/lost-found) **Terminal 2 Options** &gt; **Lost &amp; Found** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 2 - Arrivals level, behind the Airport Shuttle drop-off &amp; pick-up points at P16 / P17 &gt; You can write to **t2lostandfound@bialairport.com** or call **+91-8066785555** if you cannot find your item in the search. &gt; Please keep your **boarding pass**, a **valid Government photo ID**, and the **details of the item** ready when you claim it. &gt; If someone else is collecting it for you, they will also need their ID, your ID, your boarding pass, and an authorization letter from you. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/travellers/passenger-services/lost-found) If the item was lost **on board the flight or at the gate area**, please contact the **airline’s Lost and Found department** directly, as their process may be different.">
      <data key="d0">response</data>
      <data key="d1">Namaskara from Bangalore International A</data>
      <data key="d2">If you’ve lost something at BLR</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Namaskara from Bangalore International Airport Limited. Thank you for contacting us. I found Dewar’s options in Terminal 2. Since you asked broadly, I’m sharing the available choices I could verify for you. **Terminal 1 Options** I could not find a verified Dewar’s listing in Terminal 1 from the available information. **Terminal 2 Options** &gt; **Dewar’s 12 Years** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 2 - Level 4 - Radio House Bar &gt; This listing is available in the airport data, and it is marked as collect at store. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/storefront/60ed76aca8258362b0e5d1038a?QueryProp1=Dewar%27s%2012%20years) &gt; **Dewar’s White Label** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 2 - Level 4 - Radio House Bar &gt; This listing is available in the airport data, and it is marked as collect at store. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/storefront/60ed76aca8258362b0e5d1038a?QueryProp1=Dewar%27s%20White%20Label) &gt; **12 Year Old Twin Pack** &gt; **Zone:** Terminal 2 - Level 1 - Duty Free Departure &gt; This is a duty free collect-at-store item. &gt; **Reference:** [Click here for more details](https://www.bengaluruairport.com/storefront/64d09a82d3be5d5cec40la690dut1?QueryProp1=12%20Year%20Old%20Twin%20Pack) If you’d like, I can also help you with the exact whisky type you want, like blended whisky, single malt, or duty free twin packs.">
      <data key="d0">response</data>
      <data key="d1">Namaskara from Bangalore International A</data>
      <data key="d2">I found Dewar’s options in Terminal 2</data>
      <data key="d3">1</data>
